    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hoopers Creek hosts the Hooper's Creek Presbyterian Church, a wooden landmark that dates back to the late 18th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/north-carolina_hoopers-creek",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits in the valley of Hoopers Creek, a west‑flowing tributary of Cane Creek that feeds the French Broad River watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoopers_Creek%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Burney Mountain, rising to 2,983 feet, crowns the northern edge of the CDP, while Bank Mountain reaches 3,693 feet to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoopers_Creek%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hoopers Creek lies within the Blue Ridge Mountains and borders the Pisgah National Forest, offering a quintessential rural mountain setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/north-carolina_hoopers-creek",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area is primarily residential, with a strong focus on agriculture and outdoor recreation that reflects its mountain heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/north-carolina_hoopers-creek",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The CDP’s name, Hoopers Creek, derives from the early settlers who farmed along the creek’s banks in the 1700s.",
